> **Connection to Mental Health and MHC's Goal of Ending Stigma**
> 
> Throughout my career, I have observed the intertwined nature of sustainability, climate change, and human well-being, which includes mental health. My work has emphasized equity-focused issues, highlighting the importance of addressing stigma and promoting inclusion within communities. While my professional roles have not been directly tied to mental health organizations, my involvement in programs addressing climate adaptation and sustainable community initiatives underscores the importance of holistic well-being, including mental health aspects. Personally, I've been influenced by seeing the impacts of climate change on community health and resilience, deepening my commitment to supporting efforts that aim to destigmatize mental health challenges and foster open conversations.
> 
> **Experience Leading Organizational Change and Transformation**
> 
> Leading organizational change has been a recurring theme in my roles. At the Clean Energy Buyers Association, I spearheaded the development of the diversity, equity, and inclusion program, which represented significant internal change. This required building consensus across diverse stakeholders, crafting clear communication strategies, and aligning the program with organizational goals. I learned that successful change management hinges on transparency, active listening, and scalability. Understanding the unique pace and cultural dynamics of each organization has been crucial in identifying tailored solutions that are both ambitious and achievable.
> 
> **Building or Growing a Fundraising Program**
> 
> I have extensive experience in designing and implementing fundraising strategies. At the Institute for Market Transformation, I independently developed a stewardship strategy that led to over $50,000 in new gifts within a year. My approach involved comprehensive donor research, tailored engagement plans, and fostering long-term relationships with donors and board members. By piloting an advisory board and organizing revenue-generating events like the DC Climate Week, I increased regional investments and participation. My contributions were instrumental in expanding program-specific memberships and enhancing funding pipelines.
> 
> **Working Across Complex Stakeholder Ecosystems**
> 
> Complex stakeholder ecosystems have been a staple in my career. For instance, while working at Sustainable Ventures in London, I established an innovation hub that brought together academic, start-up, and government entities. The key to creating shared value was to align each stakeholder's intrinsic motivations with the overarching goals of the initiative. Facilitating open forums and encouraging collaborative problem-solving were crucial in managing diverse priorities. By understanding and respecting individual stakeholder needs, I was able to foster cooperation and drive collective action towards clean technology development and investment.
